1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
Using several AI models
together sounds powerful.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,000
But reliable collaboration
starts with understanding

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,000
which part of the system does what.

4
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,000
A model generates responses.

5
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,000
A harness manages the
agent's tools and context.

6
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
An orchestrator coordinates the workflow.

7
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,000
The interface is where you interact.

8
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,000
A sandbox limits what
execution can access.

9
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Imagine adding CSV export to an app.

10
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Agree on the requirements, then
let an agent implement them.

11
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Run tests, ask a separate
reviewer to find concrete defects,

12
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:40,000
and send failures back for repair.

13
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:44,000
After repairs, a fresh
verifier checks the candidate

14
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:48,000
against each original requirement.

15
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:52,000
For example: does the export
respect the selected filter?

16
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Record the evidence.

17
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Agreement alone does not
establish correctness.

18
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:01,500
LangGraph provides
workflow building blocks.

19
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:05,000
Deep Agents adds a reusable harness.

20
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:08,500
Deep Agents Code supplies
a terminal application.

21
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:12,000
An existing interface can
connect through an integration.

22
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:16,000
Start with one bounded
task, clear stopping rules,

23
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:20,000
and checks you can inspect.
Compare with a single agent.

24
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Add complexity when it earns its place.

